<title>USA: U.S. Q2 GDP revised to up 4.7 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Q2 GDP revised to up 4.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce seasonally adjusted GDP data on a chain-weighted basis. Following are annualized percent changes from prior quarters, in 1992 chain dollars.</p>
<p>    -			     Q2-F   Q2-P   Q1-F---1995</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product	4.7    4.8    2.0    2.0</p>
<p> Final Sales Domest.Product  4.1    4.3    3.0    2.4</p>
<p> GDP Price Index		 2.2    2.2    2.3    2.5</p>
<p> Implicit Price Deflator     1.8    1.8    2.2    2.5</p>
<p> Consumer Spending	     3.4    3.4    3.5    2.3</p>
<p> -Durable Goods		 11.4   11.8    8.2    3.2</p>
<p> -Nondurable Goods	     1.3    1.6    3.7    2.3</p>
<p> Pct Change,'92 chain dollars: Q2-F   Q2-P   Q1-F---1995</p>
<p> Consumer Spending-Services  2.7    2.5    2.4    2.2</p>
<p> Business Investment	   3.8    4.0   11.6    9.5</p>
<p> Housing Investment	   16.3   15.9    7.4   -2.3</p>
<p> Exports of Goods/Svcs	 5.6    4.8    1.8    8.9</p>
<p> Imports of Goods/Svcs	 9.9    9.4   10.6    8.0</p>
<p> Govt.Purchases/Investment   7.7    8.2    1.6   Unch</p>
<p> -Federal			  9.4   10.7    6.0   -3.6</p>
<p> -State and Local		6.7    6.8   -0.9    2.4</p>
<p>Note: Advance (A) is first estimate, Preliminary (P) is second estimate, and Final (F) is last estimate for the quarter.  </p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted annual rates, in blns of '92 chain dollars:</p>
<p>    -				Q2-F-----Q2-P-----Q1-F----1995</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product   6,892.6  6,894.5  6,814.3  6,742.9</p>
<p> Final Sales Dom.Product  6,884.7  6,886.4  6,815.2  6,708.9</p>
<p> Consumer Spending	  4,687.6  4,688.1  4,649.1  4,577.8</p>
<p> -Durable Goods		 615.6    616.1    599.2    579.8</p>
<p> -NonDurable Goods	  1,440.9  1,442.0  1,436.1  1,421.9</p>
<p> -Services		    2,632.3  2,631.2  2,614.7  2,577.0</p>
<p> Business Investment	  750.5    750.9    743.5    714.3</p>
<p> Housing Investment	   281.5    281.3    271.1    262.8</p>
<p>A-Advance. P-Preliminary. F-Final.  </p>
<p> Blns of '92 chain dollars:     Q2-F-----Q2-P-----Q1-F-----1995</p>
<p> Inventory Change		 7.1	7.2     -3.0     33.1</p>
<p> -NonFarm			  11.7     11.9	2.9     37.2</p>
<p> -Farm			     -5.1     -5.2     -6.5     -4.7</p>
<p> Net Exports Goods/Svcs    -114.7   -115.2   -104.0   -107.6</p>
<p> -Exports			 817.9    816.2    806.7    775.4</p>
<p> -Imports			 932.6    931.4    910.7    883.0</p>
<p> Government Purchases     1,278.2  1,279.8  1,254.7  1,260.2</p>
<p> -Federal			 473.4    474.8    462.9    472.3</p>
<p> -State and Local	     805.5    805.7    792.6    788.6</p>
<p>A-Advance. P-Preliminary. F-Final.  </p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected the final estimate of the second quarter GDP to show a 4.6 percent increase. They expected the second quarter price index to be up 2.2 percent increase, and the implicit price deflator to rise 1.8 percent.</p>
